  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts and it passes the typecheck. I couldn't run the scene or `vite build` here, so none of it has been rendered or checked visually.\n\n- **Crystals:** seven crystals are built as one custom mesh with `geometry.define`. Each has 5 or 6 sides, a pointed top, its own height and tilt, and unshared vertices with face normals for flat shading. Every side triangle and tip triangle gets its own HSL colour as a vertex colour.\n- **Rotation:** the crystal mesh has a runtime id and spins about Y each frame (`setRotation(0, t * 0.3, 0)`). It sits on a static two-layer metallic cylinder pedestal.\n- **Sparks:** two `effects.particles` emitters, gold and cyan, spawn from a disc around the cluster. They use additive blending and noise, and have no gravity, so the sparks should drift upward.\n- **Mood:** the background is near-black, with a dim blue key light, a cyan rim light and a magenta rim light from behind, and a small violet point light. Bloom and vignette are on.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set to true on the first `requestAnimationFrame` after `await app.ready()`.\n\nI'm not sure the face colours will read as clearly as intended against the dark lighting. That is the first thing I'd check in a render.\n\n",
